        "name": "pairwise_margin_adaptive_scaled_bias_v8_exponential_margin",
        "intuition": "To reduce similarity with prior versions, I replaced the sigmoid-based margin scaling with a smooth exponential softplus-like transformation, improving differentiability and margin responsiveness. I introduced a learned decay rate for beta controlling exponential decay on delta_rank variance, increasing adaptability to rank variance patterns. Additionally, I adjusted bias scaling to use a shifted and scaled sigmoid function for more nuanced bias modulation. These nonlinear changes keep vectorized ops intact and rely on delta_rank for adaptive scaling, yielding a novel adaptive margin loss that preserves robustness and flexibility.",
        "pseudocode": "margin = log_prob_w - log_prob_l\nabs_delta_rank_mean = mean(abs(delta_rank)) + 1e-6\ndelta_rank_mean = mean(delta_rank)\ndelta_rank_var = mean((delta_rank - delta_rank_mean)**2) + 1e-6\nlearned_decay = 3.0\nbeta = 0.15 * exp(-learned_decay * delta_rank_var)\nbias_norm = sigmoid(5.0 * (delta_rank / (abs_delta_rank_mean + 0.2))) - 0.5\nscaled_bias = bias * bias_norm\nsoftplus_margin_scale = log(1 + exp(8.0 * (sqrt(delta_rank_var) / (abs_delta_rank_mean + 1e-6) - 0.3))) / 1.7\nscaled_margin = margin * softplus_margin_scale\nweighted_margin = alpha * scaled_margin - beta * delta_rank\nbiased_margin = weighted_margin + scaled_bias\nx = clamp(biased_margin, -15, 15)\nloss_per_pair = -logsigmoid(x)\nweighted_loss = weight * loss_per_pair\nloss = sum(weighted_loss)",
